=   entry .Reader   a cursor over a message, reading one field at a time with its bounds checked
-     detail
+     detail

-         `Wire.Reader(data)` starts at the first byte. Each read advances the cursor and
-         raises `Wire.Error` (`Truncated`) if the message ends before the field does, or
-         (`Oversized`) if a length prefix exceeds `Wire.Limit`, before anything is allocated.
-         A `Reader` is `caps.Mutable`: its reads are `update` methods, and it should be
-         consumed by the code which made it.
+         `Wire.Reader(data)` empieza en el primer byte. Cada lectura avanza el cursor y lanza
+         `Wire.Error` (`Truncated`) si el mensaje termina antes que el campo, o (`Oversized`)
+         si un prefijo de longitud supera `Wire.Limit`, antes de reservar nada. Un `Reader` es
+         `caps.Mutable`: sus lecturas son métodos `update`, y debe consumirlo el código que lo
+         creó.

=         consumed by the code which made it.
